learn=[('Define the four tool parts', 'Give tool() a name, a useful description, a Zod input schema and an async handler. The schema types the handler arguments and validates inputs.'), ('Run a server in your application', 'createSdkMcpServer wraps the handlers in-process. The Claude Code runtime remains a child process and the model/API services are remote; in-process describes the custom MCP server.'), ('Register and approve the full name', 'mcpServers.weather supplies the namespace in mcp__weather__get_temperature. allowedTools pre-approves that name; the wildcard mcp__weather__* approves all registered weather tools.'), ('Call real weather services', 'Ask for San Francisco and Madrid. Inspect real handler arguments, HTTP status, observation times and returned content. The app uses live Open-Meteo data and never substitutes a saved forecast.'), ('Add optional parameters', 'The second tool uses hours.optional(). The handler applies args.hours ?? 12. Compare omitted hours with an explicit value of six using actual handler evidence.'), ('Wrap your own endpoint', 'A third tool calls this app’s read-only /api/course endpoint over real local HTTP. It is a classroom endpoint, so no private database or production integration is implied.')]
document('/','Your functions. <em>Claude calls them.</em>','Custom tools with typed inputs, in-process MCP and real API results.','<div class="flow"><div><b>01 · Define</b><p>Name, description, schema, handler</p></div><span>→</span><div><b>02 · Register</b><p>Server namespace and approval</p></div><span>→</span><div><b>03 · Call</b><p>Actual HTTP and handler evidence</p></div></div><section class="panel" id="controls"><h2>Call your custom tools</h2><p id="configuration" class="meta">Checking local server…</p><label for="mode">Custom-tool experiment</label><select id="mode"><option value="temperature-sf">Temperature · San Francisco</option><option value="temperature-madrid">Temperature · Madrid</option><option value="rain-default">Precipitation · omit hours → default 12</option><option value="rain-six">Precipitation · explicit hours = 6</option><option value="both">Two tools · wildcard approval</option><option value="course-api">Your API · local course endpoint</option><option value="no-approval">Permission comparison · no pre-approval</option></select><button id="run" class="primary" disabled>Run custom-tool experiment →</button><p class="meta">Seven fixed classroom tasks. Live weather needs internet access. tools: [] removes built-ins; custom MCP tools remain configured. No separate MCP server needs to be started.</p></section><div class="workspace"><section class="panel" id="outcome"><h2 id="status" aria-live="polite">Ready</h2><p>SDK reported cost: <strong id="cost">—</strong></p><p class="meta">Session: <span id="session">—</span></p><div id="answer" class="markdown-body"></div><p id="notice" class="note"></p></section><section class="panel" id="option-panel"><h2>Options actually passed</h2><pre class="json-view"><code id="options" class="language-json">{}</code></pre><p>Compare exact names, the weather wildcard and an empty pre-approval list. alwaysLoad keeps these small teaching schemas present without a separate tool-search step.</p></section></div><section class="step" id="discovery-panel"><h2>Actual available tools</h2><pre class="json-view"><code id="discovery" class="language-json">{}</code></pre></section><section class="step" id="handler-panel"><h2>Actual handler inputs and API results</h2><pre class="json-view"><code id="handlers" class="language-json">[]</code></pre><p>These entries come from real in-process handler executions, not from the model’s prose. Weather includes Open-Meteo attribution and timestamps; precipitation begins at the current UTC hour.</p></section><section class="step" id="evidence-panel"><h2>Verify calls, defaults and permission</h2><pre class="json-view"><code id="evidence" class="language-json">{}</code></pre><p>Compare omitted hours with effectiveHours: 12, then args.hours: 6 with effectiveHours: 6. In No pre-approval, the denying callback should run and the weather handler should not. A model answer alone does not prove execution.</p></section><section class="step" id="init-panel"><h2>Actual system/init projection</h2><pre class="json-view"><code id="init" class="language-json">{}</code></pre></section><section class="step" id="run-history"><h2>Compare this browser’s experiments</h2><div class="table"><table><thead><tr><th>Mode</th><th>Handlers</th><th>Count</th><th>Callback requests</th><th>Hours</th></tr></thead><tbody id="history"></tbody></table></div><button id="download">Download actual observations</button></section><section class="step" id="event-panel"><h2>Actual SDK messages</h2><ol id="events"></ol></section>','<script type="module" src="/client.js"></script>')
document('/learn.html','What you <em>will learn.</em>','Turn an application function into a tool the agent can call.',cards(learn))
env='ANTHROPIC_API_KEY=your_api_key\nCLAUDE_MODEL=claude-sonnet-4-6\nPORT=3122\n# Optional on Windows: CLAUDE_CODE_GIT_BASH_PATH=C:/Program Files/Git/bin/bash.exe'
runsteps=[('Prepare the runtime', 'Use Node.js 24 or later. On Windows the SDK runtime may require Git Bash. The custom server runs inside this app; Open-Meteo needs internet access and the model needs an API account.', 'node --version\nnpm --version'), ('Install and create your .env file', 'From presentations, run these commands. Preserve an existing .env and enter your key locally. The npm startup script loads that file; existing shell variables take precedence.', 'cd .\\agent-sdk\\lesson22-custom-tools\nnpm ci\nif (!(Test-Path .env)) { Copy-Item .env.example .env }\nnotepad .env'), ('Start the web application', 'Keep this terminal running and open the printed URL. You do not need to start a separate MCP server. Use Ctrl+C to stop this app.', 'npm start\n# http://127.0.0.1:3122'), ('Ask about two cities', 'Run San Francisco and Madrid. Compare actual handler coordinates, the live temperature and observation time. Weather changes, so there is no fixed expected number.', 'npm run sample:env -- temperature-sf\nnpm run sample:env -- temperature-madrid'), ('Compare optional hours and wildcard approval', 'Run omitted hours, explicit six hours and both tools. Inspect the original args and the handler’s applied default. The wildcard pre-approves both weather tools.', 'npm run sample:env -- rain-default\nnpm run sample:env -- rain-six\nnpm run sample:env -- both'), ('Wrap a local API and compare permission', 'Leave the web server running for course-api, which calls /api/course. No pre-approval keeps tools available but denies unresolved calls in this classroom callback.', 'npm run sample:env -- course-api\nnpm run sample:env -- no-approval\nnpm test')]
body=''
for i,(title,explanation,code) in enumerate(runsteps,1):body+=f'<section class="step" id="run-step-{i}"><span class="number">{i:02}</span><h2>{title}</h2><p>{explanation}</p>'+snippet(code,'powershell')+'</section>'
body+='<section class="step"><h2>Your .env configuration</h2>'+snippet(env,'dotenv')+'<p>Keep the actual key private. No Managed Agents agent ID or environment ID is required. No duplicate snapshot is included.</p></section><section class="note"><h3>Troubleshooting</h3><p>Use the URL printed by startup. If another app occupies the port, change PORT and restart. If API credit is unavailable, add credit to the account used by this key. Weather HTTP or validation failures remain visible; no cached result replaces a failed live call. The course-api CLI exercise requires this web server to be running on the same PORT.</p></section>'
document('/run.html','Configure and <em>run the app.</em>','Install the SDK, set your local key and call your functions.',body)
specs=[('Validate the task', 'src/agent.ts', 'return { mode:', 'Accept a listed classroom task. The browser does not choose arbitrary endpoints or define executable handlers.', 0, 1), ('Describe typed coordinates', 'src/weather.ts', 'export const coordinates =', 'Zod constrains latitude and longitude. Field descriptions help the model supply the intended values.', 1, 3), ('Define name description and handler', 'src/weather.ts', 'const getTemperature = tool(', 'tool() joins the unique name, model-readable description, schema and asynchronous handler. Handler arguments are inferred from the schema.', 1, 3), ('Add an optional parameter', 'src/weather.ts', 'hours: z', 'The second tool adds an optional integer from one through twenty-four. Optional means callers may omit it; it does not insert the default.', 1, 3), ('Apply the default inside the handler', 'src/weather.ts', 'const hours = args.hours ?? 12;', 'Use nullish coalescing inside the handler. Inspect actual args to distinguish omission from an explicit twelve or six.', 3, 3), ('Wrap tools in a server', 'src/weather.ts', 'return createSdkMcpServer({', 'The weather server contains both tool definitions and runs in the Node host process. alwaysLoad keeps these small schemas eager for this lesson.', 1, 2), ('Register the server namespace', 'src/agent.ts', 'const mcpServers:', 'Register weather or the local course server. The registration key becomes the middle segment of the fully qualified MCP tool name.', 1, 2), ('Pre-approve the intended calls', 'src/agent.ts', 'if (mode === "no-approval")', 'Use the full tool name or the weather wildcard. Empty allowedTools does not remove tools; unresolved calls reach this app’s denying callback.', 1, 2), ('Start one real SDK query', 'src/agent.ts', 'const run = query(', 'An asynchronous input generator keeps the query open for in-process MCP exchange. The SDK handles the model and tool orchestration.', 1, 2), ('Observe the actual tool request', 'src/agent.ts', 'if (block.type === "tool_use")', 'Inspect an actual assistant tool_use block. A request or answer in prose is not proof that the handler completed.', 2, 3), ('Fetch the real forecast', 'src/weather.ts', 'const response = await fetcher(', 'The handler requests a fixed Open-Meteo endpoint with a timeout and checks HTTP status. The response schema rejects malformed service data.', 3, 4), ('Return a tool content block', 'src/weather.ts', 'return { content: [{ type: "text", text: JSON.stringify(output) }] };', 'Return actual API data in the required content array. The SDK supplies this result to Claude so it can compose an answer.', 3, 2), ('Render the answer and evidence', 'src/client.ts', 'if (e.type === "answer")', 'Render and sanitize actual Markdown. Keep model text beside handler evidence, HTTP status, parameter choices and permission requests.', 1, 0)]
steps=[];arrows=[];lanes=['Student UI','Node host','SDK + Claude','MCP handler','HTTP APIs']
for n,(title,source,anchor,explanation,a,b) in enumerate(specs,1):
 text=(APP/source).read_text(encoding='utf-8');lines=text.splitlines();idx=next(i for i,l in enumerate(lines) if anchor in l)
 count={1:4,2:4,3:5,4:6,5:4,6:6,7:6,8:4,9:4,10:5,11:5,12:5,13:3}.get(n,1);code='\n'.join(lines[idx:idx+count]).strip()
 steps.append(dict(number=n,title=title,source=source,code=code,language='typescript',explanation=explanation,firstLine=idx+1,lastLine=idx+count,anchors=[lines[idx].strip()],sourceSHA256=hashlib.sha256(text.encode()).hexdigest(),narration=f'Step {n}. {explanation} This source excerpt shows the corresponding application statement.'))
 arrows.append([a,b,f'{n}. {title}'])
(APP/'scripts/architecture-data.json').write_text(json.dumps(dict(lanes=lanes,arrows=arrows,steps=steps),indent=2),encoding='utf-8')
