reference=[('In-process is specific', 'The custom MCP server and handlers run in this Node application. The SDK still uses its Claude Code runtime and calls the remote model. This is not a claim that the entire agent runs in one process.'), ('Tool search and eager teaching schemas', 'Current SDK documentation describes deferred tool search by default. This small application explicitly uses alwaysLoad: true, so all configured custom schemas are immediately available. It does not demonstrate deferred tool search.'), ('Real weather and attribution', 'Open-Meteo supplies forecast and current-condition model data. Units are Fahrenheit, times are UTC, and probability windows start at the current UTC hour. Values change between runs. Open-Meteo.com attribution is included in handler results.'), ('API exercise boundaries', 'The course tool makes a real HTTP call to this app’s public classroom endpoint. The course payload is fixed teaching data. Replacing it with your own authenticated endpoint requires implementing that handler and keeping credentials on the server.'), ('Availability and permission', 'tools: [] removes built-ins while configured MCP tools remain. allowedTools pre-approves full names or wildcards. The last experiment leaves approval empty and denies unresolved requests; denial means no handler output should be claimed.'), ('Later lessons', 'The content array can carry other block types. This lesson executes text results only. Advanced annotations, richer content and structured results are introduced later; basic service errors are surfaced without invented fallbacks.')]

document('/walkthrough.html','How the app <em>was built.</em>','Thirteen source-linked steps connect tool definition, registration and real execution.',cards(reference)+walk)
readme='# Claude Agent SDK · Lesson 22 · Custom tools and in-process MCP\n\nBased on Lesson22_Custom_Tools_In_Process_MCP.pptx. Five linked student pages with large text and coloured code in every UML step.\n\n## What you will learn\n\n'+''.join(f'- {a}: {b}\n' for a,b in learn)
readme+='\n## Configure and run\n\n```powershell\ngit clone https://github.com/luiscoco/Udemy-Claude-Agent-SDK-lesson22-app.git\ncd .\\Udemy-Claude-Agent-SDK-lesson22-app\nnpm ci\nif (!(Test-Path .env)) { Copy-Item .env.example .env }\nnotepad .env\nnpm start\n```\n\nFrom presentations use `cd .\\agent-sdk\\lesson22-custom-tools` instead of cloning. Open http://127.0.0.1:3122 and keep the terminal running. Node.js 24+, API credit, model access and internet are required. Windows may require Git Bash. No separate MCP server is needed.\n\n## Create your .env file\n\nCopy .env.example only if .env does not exist. Enter your key privately and restart after edits. The startup script loads this file; existing shell values take precedence.\n\n```dotenv\n'+env+'\n```\n\nNo Managed Agents IDs are required. Real .env, media, private workspaces and dependencies are excluded from Git.\n\n## Run the experiments\n\n'
for title,explanation,code in runsteps[3:]:readme+=f'### {title}\n\n{explanation}\n\n```powershell\n{code}\n```\n\n'
readme+='## How the app was built\n\n'
for step in steps:readme+=f'### {step["number"]}. {step["title"]}\n\n{step["explanation"]}\n\nSource: `{step["source"]}`, lines {step["firstLine"]}–{step["lastLine"]}. Selected source; surrounding code omitted.\n\n```typescript\n{step["code"]}\n```\n\n'
readme+='## Reference topics and limits\n\n'+''.join(f'- {a}: {b}\n' for a,b in reference)+'\n## References\n\n- [Custom tools: official SDK documentation](https://code.claude.com/docs/en/agent-sdk/custom-tools)\n- [Open-Meteo weather API](https://open-meteo.com/en/docs)\n- [Open-Meteo licence and attribution](https://open-meteo.com/en/licence)\n\nRegenerate student pages with `python scripts/build-pages.py`. `npm test` checks parameter boundaries, forecast slicing, HTTP failures and startup without paid model calls.\n'
(APP/'README.md').write_text(readme,encoding='utf-8')
print('Built five Lesson 22 student pages and thirteen source-linked UML steps.')
